  "summary": "The Cook County Board approved roughly $1 million for Sheriff Tom Dart to nearly double his Flock license plate reader network to 125 cameras, a day after the sheriff's office acknowledged it had operated Flock cameras for years without an active contract. The vote came amid a state audit finding Flock illegally shared data with federal immigration agents and a Texas sheriff investigating an abortion case, and as nearby Oak Park and Evanston canceled their Flock contracts.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Have we been acting without a contract? Yes, we have,",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "the agency continued to pay Flock for the service on a month-to-month basis",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "the sheriff's office cannot monitor what authorized agencies do with the data they access",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    }
  ],
